     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a likely error.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg is 5 times the maximum recommended dose.** The usual adult dose is 2.5 to 10 mg by mouth once daily, and 10 mg is the max. A 50 mg dose could cause severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia and shock. Amlodipine has a long half-life (about 30 to 50 hours), so an overdose can be hard to reverse.\n\nThe most likely explanation is a typo for **5 mg** (a common starting dose) or 10 mg.\n\nWhich do you want?\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily.** I can enter this right away.\n2. **A different dose within 2.5 to 10 mg.**\n3. **50 mg as written.** If this is really intended, please confirm and give a reason, and I'll add it to the order note. Your pharmacy will likely still need to verify it."
      }
     ],
