       "type": "text",
       "text": "I've entered the order as written: amlodipine 50 mg by mouth, once daily (Order ID: ORD-0001).\n\nI added a high-dose alert to the order note. It says 50 mg is 5 times the 10 mg maximum, that you confirmed the dose after being warned, and that no clinical reason was given. It also asks for pharmacist verification before dispensing. Pharmacy will probably contact you before releasing it.\n\nPlease consider:\n- **Adding a clinical reason** to the order, if there is one, so pharmacy and nursing can see it. I can update the note for you.\n- **Monitoring closely if the drug is given:** frequent blood pressure and heart rate checks, watching for low blood pressure, swelling or signs of shock. Amlodipine's long half-life means any effects could last for days.\n\nIf you'd like to change the dose to 5 or 10 mg, tell me and I'll enter a corrected order."
      }
